ROLE: theory_skeptic  VOTE: red
MUNDANE_EXPLANATIONS: [
  "Cold-then-hot frequency = 0.000 is fully predicted by basic transformer attention theory: early tokens in a causal context accumulate attention from ALL subsequent query positions, so an early committed handle mechanically becomes a heavy-hitter — Xiao et al. 'StreamingLLM' (2309.17453) attention-sink result, and Scissorhands persistence-of-importance (2305.17118), both predict exactly this monotonic rise. The L0's 'cold-then-hot' was the surprising claim; its absence is the boring null.",
  "H2O AUC ≈ 1.000 on the critical handle is the expected baseline behavior on any trace where one span is a persistent heavy-hitter — the eviction score IS accumulated attention, so retention of the top-ranked span is tautological, not evidence of H2O 'winning'. CAUSAL−H2O = +0.00 [0,0] across all cells reflects ceiling collinearity (lexical handle hit rate = 1.000 ⇒ proxy and H2O rank the same span #1), not a learned advantage of either.",
  "Recency-truncation = 0.00 is mechanically forced by the task design (handle committed early, queried late) and adds no signal — it is the same strawman VERDICT-0009 already flagged. Reporting it alongside H2O inflates apparent baseline coverage."
]
CONFOUNDS: [
  "Single model (Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct, eager attn, 1 size, 1 family) — cold-then-hot structure could plausibly appear in larger models, MoE, GQA with different head allocation, or sink-token-trained models. Generalizing 'real LLM attention does the opposite' from one 1.5B checkpoint is overreach in BOTH directions (overclaim for refutation, same as the L0's overclaim for confirmation).",
  "Constructed transcripts, not real tool benchmarks. The packet admits no tau-bench/AppWorld was installable (egress gated). 'Hard' design is author-judged adversarial-to-H2O, but adversariality was operationalized as 'buried handle + decoys + no primary flag' — NOT as 'engineered to suppress early attention mass'. A genuinely adversarial design would explicitly drive early attention rank into the bottom half; the observed crit early_rank ≥ 0.50 shows the hostile design did not actually stress-test the cold phase.",
  "Layer aggregation choice (mid+late, layers 14–27) is a researcher degree of freedom. H2O in practice is often per-head/per-layer; an averaged mid+late signal may smooth over heads where the handle IS briefly cold. No per-head or per-layer breakdown is shown to rule this out.",
  "Span definition uses chat-template tool-role boundaries — handle tokens may sit near a role-boundary token that itself acts as an attention sink, pulling rank up artifactually. Not tested."
]
ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED: [
  "That 1.5B-model attention geometry generalizes to the 7B–70B agents where CLAIM-0010 would actually matter. Untested.",
  "That layers 14–27 mean+sum is the right H2O-equivalent score. No ablation over layer subsets or per-head H2O.",
  "That K=2 commit-window and DELAY≥3 are the right thresholds — a stricter K=1 or larger live-span pool could still produce cold phases; sensitivity over (K, DELAY, top-quartile vs top-decile) not reported.",
  "That 'real eager attention' on a constructed transcript is equivalent to 'real tool-agent trace distribution'. The trace generator is in-house; its distribution over decoy density, handle re-mention timing, and tool-result length is not validated against a real benchmark.",
  "Prior-art subsumption argument assumes A2SF / ArkVale / Quest / Apple-Learning-to-Evict are operative on this trace family — none were run as baselines, only cited."
]
STATISTICAL_GAPS: [
  "Pass@1 CI = [0, 0] at every budget is suspicious — bootstrap CI collapses to a point when both arms produce identical per-seed outcomes. This is a degeneracy (pairs are tied), not evidence of a tight estimate. Report tie rate and McNemar discordant-pair count instead.",
  "806 spans across 40 seeds × 2 designs ⇒ ~10 spans per seed-design — the 0/806 cold-then-hot count gives a one-sided 95% upper bound (rule of three) of ≈ 0.37%, which IS below the 5% 'rare' threshold, but the packet never states the upper bound; reporting 'frequency = 0.000' without the rule-of-three CI overstates precision.",
  "No multiple-comparison correction across the 4 pre-registered honest-negative branches (N1–N4), the 6 result tables, and the layer/window sensitivity choices — pre-registration mitigates this but does not eliminate it.",
  "Variance across seeds not shown for the cold_then_hot fraction or the AUC numbers — point estimates only. Per-seed scatter would substantiate the 'monotonic 0.50→1.00' claim against the possibility that a handful of seeds drive the mean."
]
RATIONALE: The L1 is methodologically honest and the pre-registered negative branches did trigger, so the *direction* of the verdict (REFUTED → WEAKEN/KILL) is well-supported for the claim AS STATED on Qwen2.5-1.5B with this trace family. My RED is not against killing the claim — it is against the packet's framing that the kill is *general*. The mundane explanation (early-token attention-sink + Scissorhands persistence, StreamingLLM 2309.17453) predicts the observed monotonic rank rise on a small dense model with eager attention and constructed transcripts; one model, one trace generator, mid+late layer-averaged H2O score, and a degenerate CI=[0,0] are insufficient to claim the cold-then-hot phenomenon is absent in real agent workloads at scale. The kill is sound for THIS configuration; the generalization is not. Vote red on the packet's scope, concurrent with endorsing the empirical refutation at the tested scale.
